// @run
// @log 1
// @warning Unused variable `b` (prefix with `_` to suppress, or remove it)
// The unused-variable warning is DECLARED, not silenced: never reading the field is the
// whole point of this spelling, and the binding has to stay for the interner to see it.
//
// Regression (silent-class-inventory D1008), graduated from
// `error-u8-inline-shape-field-never-read.vl`.
//
// THE SAME HOLE WITH NO GENERIC IN IT, and the one whose failure was silent. An INLINE-SHAPE
// annotation carrying a `u8[]` field is interned by `internInlineShapeTy`, which — like
// `gaeEnsure`, and for the same pass-order reason — declined QUIETLY on a field it could not
// code. The binding then reached `collectAnonShapes` with no row to match and the literal's
// own syntax minted one: an i32-list field over a packed byte list, in a module that
// VALIDATED and ran.
//
// With `u8[]` coded (35) the interner has a code to return and no synthetic row is minted,
// so the annotation's rep is the one the value gets. The field is never read here on
// purpose: that is the spelling whose miscompile produced no symptom at all.
const b: { v: u8[] } = { v: [7] }
print(1)
